  {
   "slug": "hosts",
   "title": "Hosts",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Podwave is made by two friends in a spare room with a lot of cushions on the walls. We started the show to ask the questions we always wanted to ask the people who make everyday things.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:host-ada}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:host-ada}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of host Ada Lin, in violet tones\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:host-ada}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ada Lin</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ada spent ten years producing radio documentaries before starting Podwave. She does the research, books the guests and asks the follow-up questions.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:host-sam}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:host-sam}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of host Sam Okoye, in coral tones\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:host-sam}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Sam Okoye</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Sam edits every episode and writes the show notes. He is the one laughing in the background, and the one who forgets to hit record about once a season.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->",
   "featured_media": "studio-desk"
  },
  {
   "slug": "guests",
   "title": "Guests",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every guest we have had on the show, by season. Want to be one? Read the note at the bottom.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns {\"className\":\"pw-guests-grid\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns pw-guests-grid\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:guest-june}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:guest-june}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of baker June Marlow with a flour-dusted apron\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:guest-june}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">June Marlow</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Baker. Episode 24.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:guest-malik}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:guest-malik}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of forester Malik Osei with leaves behind him\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:guest-malik}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Malik Osei</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Urban forester. Episode 23.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:ep-type}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:ep-type}}\" alt=\"Cover art: big overlapping letters in violet and coral\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:ep-type}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Lena Varga</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Type designer. Episode 22.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:ep-piano}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:ep-piano}}\" alt=\"Cover art: piano keys curving into a wave\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:ep-piano}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Pieter Haan</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Piano restorer. Episode 20.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Be a guest</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are always looking for people who make, fix or look after the everyday things around us. Send a short note about what you do through the contact page. No experience with microphones needed.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "template": "page-wide"
  },
  {
   "slug": "subscribe",
   "title": "Subscribe",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Podwave is free and comes out every Tuesday. Here is how to get it.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Any podcast app</strong>: search for Podwave and press follow.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>RSS</strong>: copy our feed address into any reader.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Newsletter</strong>: one email a week with the episode and Sam's show notes.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/feed/\">RSS feed</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:contact}}\">Contact us</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons -->"
  },
  {
   "slug": "contact",
   "title": "Contact",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Questions for the listener episode, guest suggestions and corrections are all welcome.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Listener mail</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>hello@podwave.example</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Guests &amp; press</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>guests@podwave.example</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We read every message, and we answer the good questions on air.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "parent": "subscribe"
  }
 ],
 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "ep-24-the-secret-life-of-sourdough",
   "title": "Ep. 24: The secret life of sourdough",
   "date": "2026-10-20T06:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A baker who has kept the same starter alive for nineteen years explains why bread is mostly patience.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This week we visit a bakery at four in the morning to meet a starter that is older than some of our listeners. Its keeper, baker June Marlow, feeds it twice a day, takes it on holiday, and once drove it across the country in a cool box on the passenger seat.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We talk about wild yeast, why every city's bread tastes slightly different, and the one mistake almost every home baker makes in their first month.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pw-guest\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pw-guest\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:guest-june}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:guest-june}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of baker June Marlow with a flour-dusted apron\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:guest-june}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pw-kicker\"} --><p class=\"pw-kicker\">This week's guest</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">June Marlow</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Head baker at a neighbourhood bakery that has opened at 4am every day for eleven years. Owner of a nineteen-year-old starter called Doris.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"pw-timestamps\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list pw-timestamps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>00:00</code> Cold open: the bakery at 4am</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>03:12</code> How a starter is born</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>14:40</code> Why your bread is flat</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>27:05</code> Doris goes on holiday</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>38:30</code> Listener question: can you freeze a starter?</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bread is mostly waiting. The rest is just remembering to come back.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>June Marlow</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pw-links\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pw-links\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} --><h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mentioned in this episode</h4><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>The bakery's weekend bread class</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Our guide to a first loaf, written with June</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Episode 12, on fermentation and pickles</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you bake along this week, send us a photo. We will share our favourites in the next listener episode.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "season-2"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "food",
    "science"
   ],
   "featured_media": "ep-bread",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": true,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Rosa Kim",
     "content": "Doris on the passenger seat made my day.",
     "date": "2026-10-20T09:15:00",
     "email": "rosa@example.com"
    },
    {
     "author": "Tom Ansel",
     "content": "Finally understand why my loaves were flat. Thank you June!",
     "date": "2026-10-21T18:02:00",
     "email": "tom@example.com"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "ep-23-who-decides-where-the-trees-go",
   "title": "Ep. 23: Who decides where the trees go?",
   "date": "2026-10-13T06:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A city forester walks us through the maps, the arguments and the very old oak that changed a whole street plan.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every street tree has a file. It has a number, a species, a planting date and, often, a small history of complaints about leaves on cars. This week, city forester Malik Osei shows us how those files become a forest.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We go out on a planting morning, look at the shade maps that decide which neighbourhoods go first, and hear about the century-old oak that a whole road was bent around.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pw-guest\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pw-guest\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:guest-malik}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:guest-malik}}\" alt=\"Illustrated portrait of forester Malik Osei with leaves behind him\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:guest-malik}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pw-kicker\"} --><p class=\"pw-kicker\">This week's guest</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Malik Osei</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Urban forester for a mid-sized city, responsible for forty thousand street trees and at least as many opinions about them.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"pw-timestamps\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list pw-timestamps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>00:00</code> A planting morning</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>06:48</code> Shade maps and fairness</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>19:20</code> The oak that bent a road</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>31:15</code> How to ask for a tree on your street</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Want a tree outside your house? Most cities have a request form. Malik's tip: ask your neighbours to sign too.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "season-2"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "cities",
    "nature"
   ],
