  {
   "slug": "ep-20-inside-a-piano-workshop",
   "title": "Ep. 20: Inside a piano workshop",
   "date": "2026-09-22T06:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Eight thousand parts, one very patient restorer and the sound of a hundred-year-old upright waking up.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A piano has around eight thousand parts, and restorer Pieter Haan knows most of them by touch. This episode was recorded entirely inside his workshop, so you will hear the hammers, the tuning and, at the end, a very old piano playing for the first time in decades.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We talk about why pianos go out of tune (it is mostly the weather), the strange smell of old felt, and the time a family found a stack of love letters inside an upright.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"pw-timestamps\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list pw-timestamps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>00:00</code> The workshop at work</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>11:20</code> Eight thousand parts</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>24:30</code> The letters in the upright</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><code>36:50</code> The first chord</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Listen with headphones for this one. The final two minutes are just the piano, and they are worth it.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "season-2"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "music",
    "craft"
   ],
   "featured_media": "ep-piano",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
